-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261010.1~sparky9~0 (2026-10-10)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * vm.swappiness = 1 (Daniel, 2026-10-10: "vm.swappiness = 1 always"). Our explanation: a low value treats swap I/O as
    more expensive than filesystem paging; 0 is also allowed. 20261010 had left it at the kernel default (60)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261010~sparky9~0 (2026-10-10)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * No zram (Daniel): it keeps part of the user's RAM captive and does not help a machine with plenty of RAM; the edition's
    swap is an emergency swap file, switched on only under memory pressure. Removed the zram-generator configuration, the zram
    udev rule and the systemd-zram-generator dependency; vm.swappiness and vm.page-cluster are back to the kernel defaults

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261009.1~sparky9~0 (2026-10-09)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * vm.max_map_count keeps SteamOS's value, with the reason for stereo: a game keeps the second eye's buffers and can map more regions than in 2D

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261009~sparky9~0 (2026-10-09)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First release: kernel tunables as user-space files instead of kernel patches
  * Sysctl: 15 keys, including kernel.kexec_load_disabled = 1
  * ntsync module and device permission, THP defrag and shrinker, zram swap, block read-ahead and BFQ for rotating disks
  * Low-latency audio: rtprio and nice limits, cpu_dma_latency, rtc0 and hpet for the audio group
